{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You</b> — the sense is: You alone are awesome. And the one [word] suffices, as in its parallel: \"YHWH as a refuge, You were for us.\" For \"YHWH as a refuge, You were for us\" would have sufficed, and similarly \"from of old,\" like \"from of old He appointed him.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 76, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:40.279912828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}